    "summary": "For a listed row, `ambient` reads only `prop.parent`. The checker lane sets `parent` only when the first declaration is an interface, so a React-declared member whose first declaration is a type literal (or whose `parent` is None) is never marked ambient.",
    "failure_scenario": "In the checker lane, `parent=None` and `declarations=[@types/react HTMLAttributes]`. The body reads `onClick`, so `decide` makes it a full typed row instead of naming it in the layer's `used` list. The structural lane may decide differently, so the two lanes diverge."
